    "lca_discussion": "\n\n## Product Component Notes\nnd carrier; and additives, which ass, arious sealant properties. The produc, ackaged for distribution to the custo, implified version of this process is sh, igure 1., nvironment and health during manufa, roducts are manufactured in the Unite\n\n## LCA Notes\nThe EPD is declared as cradle-to-gate, and hence only modules A1 to A3 are declared. In the case of use\nof secondary materials the impact of the life-cycle of these materials is considered to occur in the module\nin which they enter the PPG process. Likewise losses and disposal of waste are accounted for in the module\nin which they occur. Infrastructure processes (e.g. industrial plants, roads and vehicles) are included in all\nmodules. Module A1 includes all processes necessary for the manufacture of the raw materials for the\nsealant products. Module A2 includes the transportation of the raw materials to the PPG plant. Module\nA3 includes all processing at the PPG plant, as well as the manufacture and transportation of the packaging\nfor the finished products and disposal of all waste. The manufacture and transportation for packaging of\nthe raw materials and primary packaging is not included in the system boundary. Table 3 shows the\nmodules included in the life cycle assessment underpinning this EPD.\nTable 3 - System boundaries and modules included\n\nReplacement\n\nRefurbishment\n\nMND MND MND MND MND MND MND MND MND\n\nReference Service Life\n\nRepair\n\nB6 Operational Energy Use of\nBuilding Integrated System\nDuring Product Use\nB7 Operational Water Use of\nBuilding Integrated System\nDuring Product Use\n\nReuse, Recovery, Recycling\nPotential\n\nB5\n\nDisposal\n\nB4\n\nWaste processing\n\nB3\n\nTransport\n\nB2\n\nDeconstruction\n\nB1\n\nMaintenance\n\nMND\n\nUSE STAGE\n\nUse\n\nAssembly/Install\n\nMND\n\nManufacturing\n\nA5\n\nTransport\n\nA4\n\nTransport from gate to site\n\nCradle\nto\ngrave\n\nA1 A2 A3\n\nRaw material supply\n\nPRODUCT CONSTRU